course: dictionary
lesson: 2048
title: One word, many links
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word connection is a noun, and it has more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. In «a loose connection in the wire», connection means a place where two things are joined. In «There is a connection between sleep and good marks», it means a link between two things.
explain: Context clues tell you which meaning to use. In «We missed our connection», the word means a train, bus or plane that you change to on a journey. In «He got the job through connections», it means people you know who can help you.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try "link" or "joined" and see whether it still makes sense. The sentence tells you which meaning is right, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Connection is a noun, and its plural is connections.
fact: A connection can be a physical join, like a wire that joins to a bulb.
fact: A connection can also be a link between ideas, facts or events.
fact: «A bad connection» means a weak link to the internet or a phone network.
fact: In the plural, «connections» means people who can help you get something.
exercise: «The bulb went out because of a loose connection in the wire.» What does connection mean here? | A link to a website | A feeling of closeness between people | *A place where two things are joined | A train you change to on a journey
exercise: «We missed our connection at the station.» What is a connection here? | A weak Wi-Fi signal | A kind feeling between friends | A place where two wires join | *A train, bus or plane you change to on a journey
exercise: «He got the job through connections.» What does connections mean? | Wires joined to a power supply | Small pieces of a film | *People you know who can help you | Nerve cells in the brain
test: «Wifi can work while the house's internet connection is down.» What does connection mean here? | A place where two things are joined | A train you change to | A feeling of closeness | *A link to the internet, a phone network or a power supply
test: Ella says «There is a connection between sleep and good marks» means sleep and marks are joined by a wire. What is the best answer? | *No, it means a link between two ideas or facts | Yes, they are friends | Yes, a wire joins them | No, it means they are on the same train
exam: Your brain has about 86 billion nerve cells, each linked to thousands of others. What is a connection between two nerve cells? | *A link where two nerve cells join and pass messages | A train you change to | A feeling of closeness between people | A padlock on a website
